<!-- Tabler "bulb", filled, 24 dp: the SVG from tabler/tabler-icons, path data unmodified.
     MIT, (c) Paweł Kuna.

     The lit half of the pair. Same 24 grid and same "0 0 24 24" viewBox as ic_bulb.xml, so this is
     the second of the two drawables here that get none of the 960-grid group translate the seven
     Material Symbols do — see that file, and docs/ui.md, "Icons".

     Where the outline is one stroked construction, the filled variant is seven filled paths: each
     ray is its own rounded shape and the glass is one more, which is how Tabler builds a filled
     glyph and why there is no stroke on any of them. The svg carries fill="currentColor" at the
     root rather than on the paths, so the fill lands on each of the seven here.

     It is the shape and not only the hue that says a lamp is on — the tint changes with it, but the
     blue light filter is on the wall permanently and warms everything, so the silhouette is what is
     actually being read from four metres. -->
